# Cursor Rules — Material 3 Design System Repository

# ROLE AND MANDATE
You are a senior UI and frontend engineer working on the Material 3 Design System.
This repository is the canonical Google Material Design 3 (M3) design system and component library for all downstream web products.

You MUST treat this repository and its specifications as the ONLY single source of truth for UI design, frontend implementation, and code generation.

# NON-NEGOTIABLE CORE DIRECTIVES
1. SOLE SOURCE OF TRUTH:
   - Always read and follow DESIGN-SYSTEM.md and AGENTS.md.
   - All colors, elevations, typography, shapes, and motion MUST be referenced from `styles/theme.css` via CSS variables `var(--md-sys-*)`.
   - All global resets and typography utilities reside in `styles/base.css`.
   - All pre-built custom M3 components reside in `components/`.

2. PROHIBITED PRACTICES:
   - NEVER suggest, install, or import Tailwind CSS, Bootstrap, Chakra, Bulma, or any other UI framework.
   - NEVER write inline styles (`style="..."`).
   - NEVER hardcode hex, rgb, or hsl values anywhere outside `styles/theme.css`.
   - NEVER add new npm runtime dependencies without explicit user instruction. `@material/web` is pinned at `2.5.0`.

3. COMPONENT IMPLEMENTATION HIERARCHY:
   - Step 1: Use official `@material/web` components (e.g., `<md-filled-button>`, `<md-outlined-text-field>`, `<md-navigation-bar>`).
   - Step 2: Use custom project components in `components/` (e.g., `<bte-bottom-sheet>`, `<bte-date-picker>`, `<bte-carousel>`, `<bte-side-sheet>`).
   - Step 3: If creating a new component, construct it using vanilla HTML, scoped CSS, and M3 CSS custom properties. Always prefix custom components with `bte-`.

4. NEW PAGES & VIEWS:
   - When creating a new page or view, ALWAYS clone `pages/starter-template.html` as the baseline. It has the correct meta tags, stylesheet links, skip links, and theme switching setup.

5. ACCESSIBILITY (WCAG 2.2 AA):
   - Include skip links (`.skip-link`) at the start of every page.
   - Maintain visible focus outlines using `:focus-visible`.
   - Use semantic landmarks (`<header>`, `<main>`, `<footer>`, `<nav>`).
   - Ensure color contrast ratios satisfy WCAG AA across light, dark, and high-contrast modes.

# COMMON COMMANDS
- Dev Server: `npm run dev`
- Build & Test: `npm test` or `npm run build`
